  "final_message": "I cannot directly rename `totalCents` to `amountCents` and `placedAt` to `createdAt` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) because doing so violates **ARCH-4** from [`GEMINI.md`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/GEMINI.md):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why this is blocked\n- Renaming or removing existing fields (`totalCents`, `placedAt`) on [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) would break deployed consumers in external repositories (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`).\n\n### Compliant Migration Path Under ARCH-4\nTo rename these fields without violating ARCH-4, the change must be **additive** and follow a deprecation cycle:\n1. **Additive Phase**: Introduce `amountCents` and `createdAt` as new fields in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and populate both the old and new fields in [`orderPlaced()`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59). Mark `totalCents` and `placedAt` with `@deprecated`.\n2. **Consumer Migration**: Update downstream consumers (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`) to read `amountCents` and `createdAt`.\n3. **Removal Phase**: Remove the deprecated fields in a subsequent release after all deployed consumers have migrated.\n",
